# Verified job board API requests.
# Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request".
# Each entry notes when it was checked and what we learned from the real response.

### Greenhouse: job list (Addepar)
# Verified 2026-10-29: 200 OK, 114 jobs.
# Board token is "addepar1", not "addepar". Always confirm the token from a job URL.
# Fields used: id (posting id, appears in absolute_url), title, location.name,
# absolute_url, first_published (posted date). updated_at changes on any edit, so we ignore it.
GET https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/addepar1/jobs

### Greenhouse: job list with descriptions (Addepar)
# Verified 2026-10-29: same 114 jobs, plus content, departments, and offices per job.
# content is HTML stored as escaped text (&lt;p&gt;), and some entities are escaped
# twice (&amp;amp;). Unescape, strip tags, then unescape again to get plain text.
GET https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/addepar1/jobs?content=true

### Greenhouse: job detail (Addepar)
# Verified 2026-10-29: identical to the same job's entry in the content=true list.
# get_job uses this endpoint, so searches don't download every description.
# A Greenhouse job (internal_job_id) can have several posts (id). The SLC and Edinburgh
# AddeGrad posts share a title but are separate jobs. We track posts by id.
GET https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/addepar1/jobs/8756273002

### Lever: job list (Zoox, used as a test case only)
# Verified 2026-10-29: 200 OK, bare JSON list (no wrapper object), 229 postings.
# Fields used: id (UUID string), text (title), categories.allLocations, hostedUrl,
# createdAt (milliseconds since 1970, UTC), workplaceType ("onsite" and "hybrid" seen;
# docs say "on-site"). Descriptions are always included; there's no switch to turn them off.
GET https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/zoox?mode=json

### Lever: pagination check
# Verified 2026-10-29: returns [], so the request above already returns every posting.
GET https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/zoox?mode=json&skip=229&limit=10

### Lever: job detail (Zoox)
# Verified 2026-10-29: same data as the list item. "<" arrives as \u003C (JSON escaping,
# undone by the JSON parser), unlike Greenhouse's &lt; (HTML escaping, undone by us).
# descriptionPlain is only the intro; responsibilities and qualifications are in
# lists[].content, which is HTML only.
GET https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/zoox/0a22d356-f7f7-4374-b393-55637772edda?mode=json
### Ashby: job list (Deepgram)
# Verified 2026-10-29: 200 OK, {"jobs": [...], "apiVersion": "1"}, 80 postings, ~1.4 MB.
# Fields used: id (UUID string), title, location + secondaryLocations[].location, jobUrl,
# publishedAt (ISO, UTC), workplaceType ("Remote"/"OnSite"/"Hybrid"/null) with isRemote
# as fallback. descriptionPlain is complete and the HTML isn't escaped.
# No public detail endpoint: /posting-api/job-board/deepgram/{id} returns 401.
GET https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/deepgram

### Ashby: job list with compensation (Deepgram)
# Verified 2026-10-29: adds a "compensation" object per posting. Not used.
GET https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/deepgram?includeCompensation=true

### Wrong slug, one per ATS
# Verified 2026-10-29: all return 404. Greenhouse and Lever send a JSON body;
# Ashby sends plain text "Not Found", so check the status before parsing JSON.
GET https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/not-a-real-board-xyz/jobs

###
GET https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/not-a-real-board-xyz?mode=json

###
GET https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/not-a-real-board-xyz
